From 83555772ef78525f5259489ec79a04ed2a0da1de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode <opencode@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:54:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] RG DS Plus on BananaLinux: both panels, and its pad

The RG DS Plus drives two 1024x768 MIPI-DSI panels. KMS took only the
first connected connector, so one panel was dark; give Kms a panel each:
it finds every connected connector, orders them with the top one first
(banana-ui's BANANA_TOP, DSI-2), makes a GBM surface per panel and flips
both CRTCs. The second surface goes to the renderer's existing second
window, so one screen draws on each panel by itself, and one-panel
handhelds are unchanged.

Its buttons come from the rocknix-singleadc-joypad driver, whose evdev
name is also retrogame_joypad (vendor 484b), so it was numbered as an
RK3566 handheld and X, Y, L and R landed nowhere. Number it as itself:
the face buttons are the standard gamepad codes and select, start, F and
the sticks' buttons are the usual 314 to 318.
